# Verifies builtin-cap-env-has? returns Int(1) when a cap IS present in the env dict.
# Uses the new env-dict protocol: builtin-cap-env-has? takes a flat Dict<String, thunk>
# directly (no scope arena needed).
[call [fn [let]
  [env: [%cwd: %cwd]]
  [result: [builtin-cap-env-has? "%cwd" env]]
  result]]
=== out
Int(1)
